From 8febddb786dc50912c79de9d52a15673fc85c8de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:52:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] hostgap: cheaper host-side planning inputs

The host traces of patches 0001-0003 show the blocking reads gone but the
host still on the critical path between learning the previous verify's
lengths and launching the draft and verify graphs. The arithmetic that
replaced the reads sits on that path: torch CPU ops for the draft
kv_indptr rows and the verify plan inputs, plus about ten small device
ops for the custom-mask offsets.

The host-side plan inputs are now computed with numpy, and
fast_verify_plan uploads the custom-mask bit and byte offsets, which
plan() derives on the device, in one pinned copy before the same
segment_packbits kernel. All values are integers computed from the same
lengths; SGLANG_HOSTGAP_VALIDATE=1 also checks the uploaded bit offsets
against the device computation. No new flag: only the flagged paths of
0001-0003 change.
